#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# random_seed

#% text
# `random_seed()` gives the seed of the session generator, so that `seed(random_seed())` at the start of a later run reproduces the same draws.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
seed(42); random_seed()
#% output
#= 42

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Reproduce a run:

#% cell
{ seed(7); let s = random_seed(); let a = random_real(); seed(s); a == random_real() }
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `seed`, `random_real`, `random_integer`
